        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9fb680d8-5852-5e22-879a-8f9430ba32db",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Fireworks incident, 2014 KNVB Cup final\n- Places: De Kuip, Rotterdam\n- Organizations: AFC Ajax, PEC Zwolle, VAK410, Manchester United\n- People: Edwin van der Sar, Kenneth Vermeer, Anders Lindegaard, David de Gea\n- Roles: Goalkeeper, marketing director\n\nFacts:\n- On Easter Sunday, 20 April 2014, the Fireworks incident occurred at De Kuip in Rotterdam during the KNVB Cup final between AFC Ajax and PEC Zwolle.\n- In the early minutes of the 2014 KNVB Cup final, Ajax hooligan firm VAK410 twice threw large amounts of fireworks, flares, and smoke bombs onto the pitch around Ajax goalkeeper Kenneth Vermeer.\n- After a 30-minute recess during the 2014 Fireworks incident, Ajax marketing director Edwin van der Sar addressed the crowd, and AFC Ajax then lost 5–1 to PEC Zwolle.\n- Edwin van der Sar, born 29 October 1970, is a Dutch former professional footballer who played as a goalkeeper.\n- After winning Goalkeeper of the Year awards in Denmark and Norway in 2010, Anders Lindegaard signed for Manchester United and spent five years as a backup to Edwin van der Sar and David de Gea.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d2629872-8ac3-55eb-ba98-4f7b9c3cc4d6",
        "text": "Page: Fireworks incident. Sentence: The Fireworks incident (Dutch, \"Vuurwerkincident\") was a very serious case of Football hooliganism which took place on Easter Sunday, 20 April 2014 in De Kuip, Rotterdam, during the KNVB Cup final match between AFC Ajax and PEC Zwolle.\nPage: Fireworks incident. Sentence: Mass amounts of fireworks, flares and smoke bombs were launched into the penalty box around Ajax goalkeeper Kenneth Vermeer in the early minutes of the match, which had been thrown onto the pitch by the Ajax hooligan firm VAK410 twice in the early build up of the game.\nPage: Fireworks incident. Sentence: After a 30 minute recess in which marketing director Edwin van der Sar addressed the crowd, Ajax would go on to lose the match 5–1 to Zwolle.\nPage: Edwin van der Sar. Sentence: Edwin van der Sar OON (] ) (born 29 October 1970) is a Dutch former professional footballer who played as a goalkeeper.\nPage: Anders Lindegaard. Sentence: After winning the Goalkeeper of the Year award in both Denmark and Norway in 2010, Lindegaard was signed by Manchester United, where he played for five years as a back-up to Edwin van der Sar and David de Gea.",
